    ":question/id": "0efc2e50-f7fe-5d96-9ccf-9a091a1c5eb4",
    ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 5 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{23}=0$?",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{23}=-8+(-2)\\cdot (-4)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D &=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 5 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5 & -8 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 5 & 9 \\\\ -19 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3}.\n$$"
  },
