    ":question/id": "7857cadc-8c2c-5686-bf69-70edfa35aa94",
    ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -10 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{22}=0$?",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$\n\nThe entry in row $3$, column $2$ is $0$. Switching rows $2$ and $3$ therefore makes $a_{22}=0$.\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C &=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -10 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -10 & 6 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$"
  },
