    ":question/id": "9bfe1196-2e7e-5988-968f-9ba97eed02ca",
    ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{32}=0$?",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{32}=-2+(-2)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -15\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2}.\n$$"
  },
