    ":question/id": "cd4bff0f-670a-5112-8f69-27572c3ddbeb",
    ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 9 \\\\ -9 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{22}=0$?",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThe entry in row $1$, column $2$ is $0$. Switching rows $2$ and $1$ therefore makes $a_{22}=0$.\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 9 \\\\ -9 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 8 & 6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{1}.\n$$"
  },
