    ":question/id": "d2291842-3bd2-5a86-9d70-eec63961e717",
    ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 9 & -9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{32}=0$?",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe entry in row $2$, column $2$ is $0$. Switching rows $3$ and $2$ therefore makes $a_{32}=0$.\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X &=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 9 & -9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 9 & -9 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}\u2194{R}_{2}.\n$$"
